# Developer Reference

This folder holds **copy-and-adapt examples** for the platform features this service was generated with.

- Nothing in this folder is compiled. It is documentation, not product code.
- Copy a snippet into your own feature folder under `src/{{ model.names.namespace }}/Domains/` and change the names.
- Examples for optional features (OData, Sanitization) appear only when that feature was selected when the service was generated.

## Examples in this service

- [`Authentication.md`](Authentication.md): Cognito and other OIDC providers, policies and admin groups
{{- if model.manifest.database != null }}
- [`Database.md`](Database.md): PostgreSQL settings, password rotation, health checks, tables and EF migrations
{{- end }}
{{- if model.manifest.tenant_ready }}
- [`Tenancy.md`](Tenancy.md): the tenants table, tenant management API, tenant entities, background work and what to avoid
- [`GoingMultiTenant.md`](GoingMultiTenant.md): step by step, from one customer to several
{{- end }}
{{- for module in model.selected_modules -}}
{{- if (module.name | string.downcase) == "odata" }}
- [`OData.md`](OData.md): paginated list endpoints with `$top`, `$skip` and `$count`
{{- end -}}
{{- if (module.name | string.downcase) == "sanitization" }}
- [`Sanitization.md`](Sanitization.md): cleaning user input to prevent XSS
{{- end -}}
{{- end }}

## Ground rules

- Examples follow the standards in `.claude/guides/PERVAXIS_STANDARDS.md`.
- The package behind each example is the source of truth. If an example and the package disagree, trust the package and tell the platform team.
- Keep domain code in `Domains/`. Do not edit `Program.cs` to wire a feature. Raise a platform ticket instead.
